        <mxCell id="d-notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*1 The file system is Single-AZ&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The second subnet exists because AWS Managed Microsoft AD needs two&lt;br&gt;AZs. The file system, both clients and the Lambda function sit in the&lt;br&gt;first subnet&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*2 The network origin of the S3 Access Points is the VPC&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Lambda inside the VPC reaches it through the S3 gateway endpoint. The&lt;br&gt;artifacts bucket goes through the same endpoint&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*3 Passwords are resolved from Secrets Manager secrets&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read when AWS Managed Microsoft AD and the ONTAP fsxadmin account are&lt;br&gt;created; both clients also fetch it at run time. Operations ran&lt;br&gt;through AWS Systems Manager Run Command" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;strokeColor=#232F3E;fillColor=#FFFFFF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=4;spacingLeft=16;spacingTop=10;fontSize=16;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1">
